<xml>
  <block type="st_sd" x="20" y="20">
    <mutation uid="card42" />
    <field name="NAME">card</field>
    <field name="CS">10</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="480" h="240">Purpose: Create a grayscale BMP with selected palette levels and append calculated shades. Values must fit the chosen output range.
Wiring: SPI SD card: CS D10; SPI MOSI D11, MISO D12, SCK D13; CS as listed. Common GND; use each module’s required supply.
Try: Change the number of palette shades and the pixel formula together.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="350" y="25">
    <field name="TYPE">uint16_t</field>
    <field name="VAR">grayLevels</field>
    <value name="VALUE">
      <block type="math_number">
        <field name="NUM">256</field>
      </block>
    </value>
    <next>
      <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="350" y="25">
        <field name="TYPE">uint16_t</field>
        <field name="VAR">width</field>
        <value name="VALUE">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">65</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <next>
          <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="350" y="25">
            <field name="TYPE">uint16_t</field>
            <field name="VAR">height</field>
            <value name="VALUE">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">32</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create height as uint16_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
          </block>
        </next>
        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create width as uint16_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
      </block>
    </next>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Create grayLevels as uint16_t. Outside a body it is global; inside a function/setup/loop it belongs to that body. Its value input is the initial value.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="25" y="140">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="st_bmp_stream_create">
        <field name="DEVICE">card42</field>
        <field name="RESERVE">false</field>
        <value name="PATH">
          <block type="text">
            <field name="TEXT">GRAY.BMP</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="WIDTH">
          <block type="variables_get">
            <field name="VAR">width</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="HEIGHT">
          <block type="variables_get">
            <field name="VAR">height</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="LEVELS">
          <block type="variables_get">
            <field name="VAR">grayLevels</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <next>
          <block type="controls_if">
            <value name="IF0">
              <block type="st_sd_ok">
                <field name="DEVICE">card42</field>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">True when the most recent operation on this card succeeded. Check it before using data from a read or continuing a file write.</comment>
              </block>
            </value>
            <statement name="DO0">
              <block type="controls_for">
                <field name="VAR">pixel</field>
                <value name="FROM">
                  <block type="math_number">
                    <field name="NUM">0</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="TO">
                  <block type="math_arithmetic">
                    <field name="OP">MINUS</field>
                    <value name="A">
                      <block type="math_arithmetic">
                        <field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field>
                        <value name="A">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">width</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <value name="B">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">height</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="B">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">1</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="BY">
                  <block type="math_number">
                    <field name="NUM">1</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <statement name="DO">
                  <block type="st_bmp_append_pixel">
                    <field name="DEVICE">card42</field>
                    <value name="WHITE">
                      <block type="math_modulo">
                        <value name="DIVIDEND">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">pixel</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <value name="DIVISOR">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">grayLevels</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Keep the remainder after division. This is useful for wrapping a counter or animation position back to the beginning.</comment>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Append the next pixel in scan order. The image writer packs the file format as it streams, so the complete image need not fit in RAM.</comment>
                  </block>
                </statement>
                <next>
                  <block type="st_bmp_stream_finish">
                    <field name="DEVICE">card42</field>
                    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="160">Finish and close the image file after all expected pixels. An incomplete scan is reported as an error rather than a complete image.</comment>
                  </block>
                </next>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Repeat the body with pixel taking each value from the start to the end, using the given step. Array indices start at zero.</comment>
              </block>
            </statement>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </statement>
  </block>
</xml>
